    "title": "Eric Swalwell addresses peace initiatives and gun policy in recent posts",
    "text": "Rep. Eric Swalwell, a member of the U.S. Congress representing California’s 14th district since 2013, recently shared a series of statements on his social media account addressing issues ranging from gun control to threats against his family.\nOn September 16, 2025, Swalwell posted: “Read this plea for peace. I will stand with President Trump if he’s willing to do this. And I bet you’ll be surprised at who else will join me.”\nLater that day, he commented on gun policy by writing: “Kash Patel is NOT wrong here. An assault weapons ban will reduce mass shootings.” This post aligns with ongoing debates in Congress about the effectiveness of an assault weapons ban in curbing gun violence.\nIn another message posted on September 16, 2025, Swalwell criticized law enforcement actions in Florida: “This is rich. AG Bondi has REFUSED to prosecute MULTIPLE direct death threats against me and my family.”\nEric Swalwell has been serving in Congress since replacing Pete Stark in 2013 and represents constituents from California’s East Bay area. Born in Sac City, Iowa in 1980, Swalwell now resides in Livermore. He holds a BA from the University of Maryland, College Park (2003) and a JD from the University of Maryland, Baltimore (2006).",
